+# GridSense follow-up: source preparation and reference controls
+
+Completed on 14 October 2026 by Codex (automated). Application version: 0.4.4.
+
+## Preserved checkpoint
+
+The reviewed ZIP was preserved before this work. Its 27,217,913 bytes have
+SHA-256 `4c1d625a3c100002720ab3d58110dc71ba5fa92a85fb8baefa19920dfd2532ff`.
+The initial review's complete verification is archived under
+[checkpoint checks](verification/review-2026-10-14/checkpoint-checks/verification.json).
+The [initial review](REVIEW_2026-10-14.md) retains its dependency audits,
+packaging fixes and extracted-package smoke record.
+
+## Reproduced findings and changes
+
+| Finding | Reproduction | Change |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Git could stage runtime data outside the default directory. | An actual SQLite database, WAL and SHM in `backend/local-data/` were eligible for staging. | `.gitignore` excludes `.sqlite`, `.sqlite3` and `.db` files and their journals anywhere. Seven Git regressions cover databases, CSV staging and configuration fingerprints. |
+| Git changed two archived CSV files' bytes. | Default text normalization replaced their original CRLF line endings in the Git index. Their numerical contents did not change. | `.gitattributes` preserves recorded experimental CSVs byte for byte. The index was renormalized; production CSV working files retain their checkpoint hashes. |
+| Reference settings needed a complete, isolated comparison. | Original defaults retain the three Load 675b mismatches and active-power balance mismatch. | A fresh native process runs each of four configurations against the same 56 frozen targets. Four native regressions check the load law, preserved defaults and rejection of altered results. |
+
+Git ignore/attribute configuration is now part of the verified-input
+fingerprint, so weakening either protection requires fresh verification.
+The [Git export record](verification/followup-2026-10-14/git-source.json)
+checks every signed source/configuration/evidence file against a staged Git
+archive. Built frontend assets remain separately verified for the release ZIP.
+
+## Electrical result
+
+| Diagnostic configuration | Passed checks |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Native defaults | 52/56 |
+| Tighter convergence only | 53/56 |
+| Wider 675b constant-power window only | 56/56 |
+| Both controls | 56/56 |
+
+The three 675b differences follow the native load model's upper-voltage
+impedance branch. Tight convergence removes the balance mismatch; the solved
+load-window configuration also changes the numerical residual. The original
+simulation inputs, frozen targets and acceptance tolerances remain intact.
+The 56/56 outcomes describe explicitly changed diagnostic contexts.
+[Study design, interpretation and reproduction](REFERENCE_SENSITIVITY.md).
+
+The saved study is checked against actual native execution by
+`scripts/verify.py`. This post-hoc comparison establishes the effect of the
+declared settings in the healthy reference circuit. It does not establish
+field-grid or restoration validity, or justify silently changing production
+physics. The independent model-aware report also retains its separate scope.
