+# Reference settings sensitivity
+
+This post-hoc study isolates the settings behind the four original electrical
+reference mismatches. It applies the same 29 voltage and 27 supplementary
+targets to each complete configuration. The frozen target values and tolerances
+are retained. Each configuration runs in a separate native worker process.
+
+| Configuration | Load 675b VMaxpu | Convergence tolerance | Checks passed | Failed comparisons |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| Native defaults | 1.05 | 1e-4 | 52/56 | 675b current/P/Q; active-power balance |
+| Precision only | 1.05 | 1e-8 | 53/56 | 675b current/P/Q |
+| Wider constant-power window | 1.10 | 1e-4 | 56/56 | None |
+| Both controls | 1.10 | 1e-8 | 56/56 | None |
+
+[Complete results](../experiments/reference_sensitivity_results/results.json)
+record every comparison, actual settings, load voltage/power, residuals, source
+hashes and native solver identity. [Runner](../experiments/run_reference_sensitivity.py).
+
+## Interpretation
+
+Load 675b operates above its native VMaxpu of 1.05. The documented native
+load model uses an impedance branch above that threshold, explaining why
+actual P/Q differ from the comparator's constant-power expectations.
+[DSS load documentation](https://dss-extensions.org/dss-format/Load.html).
+The native regression independently checks that its power follows
+`nominal_kw × (voltage_on_load_base_pu / vmaxpu)²` within the existing numerical
+allowance. In the wider-window context the same operating voltage remains
+inside the constant-power window, and actual power matches its nominal target.
+
+Precision alone removes the active-power balance mismatch. Changing the load
+window also brings that residual inside the frozen allowance in this case;
+the residual depends on the solved configuration. Tight convergence reduces
+both models' active/reactive residuals below 1e-5 kW/kvar. It does not remove
+the constitutive-model differences under the native load window.
+
+The 56/56 results belong to explicitly changed diagnostic models. Production
+simulation inputs retain native defaults. The original primary comparison
+therefore remains 52/56. This study adds evidence about the causes and the
+effect of explicit settings, rather than promoting a changed configuration
+as the original model. A production model revision would need its own
+versioned inputs, acceptance criteria and affected experimental reruns.
+
+These settings were selected after inspecting existing failures. The study
+is a diagnostic control, not an unseen confirmatory experiment. Current
+targets are derived from published voltages/PQ; balance is internal numerical
+consistency. Full voltage agreement does not validate field devices, added
+ties, protection, operating ratings or restoration behavior.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+```bash
+python experiments/run_reference_sensitivity.py --output var/reference-sensitivity.json
+python experiments/run_reference_sensitivity.py --verify-report experiments/reference_sensitivity_results/results.json
+```
+
+The runner refuses changed frozen targets, checks actual configuration
+agreement across voltage and supplementary solves, and compares saved
+source/settings/results with a fresh native execution. Regression cases
+reject relabelled baseline status, forged counts and changed tolerances.
+The standard verification runner includes this check.
